# NoorLife — Supabase configuration
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values from your Supabase project
# (Project Settings -> API). Never commit .env.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL must be the project URL — the origin only, with no
# path:
#
#   correct    https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
#   wrong      https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/rest/v1/
#
# supabase-js appends its own paths (/auth/v1/..., /rest/v1/...), so a URL that
# already carries one makes every request hit an endpoint that does not exist.
# That failure surfaces as a 404 "Invalid path specified in request URL", which
# reads like a server problem rather than a typo. The client trims a stray path
# and warns in development, but set it correctly here.
#
# Only the PUBLISHABLE (anon) key belongs in this file. Anything prefixed
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ is inlined into the JavaScript bundle at build time and is
# readable by anyone with the APK, so the service-role key must never be set as
# an EXPO_PUBLIC_ variable or placed in this application at all.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
